###############################################################################
# STORE API — BASELINE REGRESSION COLLECTION
#
# This is the safety net for the whole microservices migration (docs/MIGRATION.md).
# The repo has one `contextLoads` test, so this file is what tells you whether a
# phase broke something. Run it end to end after every phase.
#
# FORMAT: VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request"
#         above each block, or run them top to bottom — later requests reuse the
#         tokens and IDs captured by earlier ones via the `# @name` references.
#         For IntelliJ's HTTP Client, replace `{{login.response.body.$.token}}`
#         with a `{% client.global.set(...) %}` post-script block.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Run sections 1 → 9 in sequence on a fresh database.
#
# ─── ONE-TIME SETUP BEFORE FIRST RUN ────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Start the app (./mvnw spring-boot:run) so Flyway builds the schema.
#      Alternatively: docker compose up --build, then
#      mysql --protocol=TCP -h 127.0.0.1 -P 3307 -u root -p store_api < docs/seed-baseline.sql
#   2. Run section 1.1 and 1.2 below (registers both accounts).
#   3. mysql -u root -p store_api < docs/seed-baseline.sql
#      ...which seeds categories and promotes admin@baseline.test to ADMIN.
#      Neither is reachable through the API — see the comments in that file.
#   4. Run everything from section 2 onward.
#
# ─── FIXED IN PHASE 1 (was an expected failure through Phase 0) ──────────────
#   • 2.4 POST /auth/refresh with no cookie now returns 400, not 401.
#     PlatformSecurityRules permits /error, so Boot's ERROR dispatch is no longer
#     re-authorized and masked. Any unhandled exception on a public endpoint now
#     surfaces its real status.
#   • The refresh cookie's Secure flag is now app.cookie.secure (COOKIE_SECURE);
#     it defaults to false on the dev profile and in docker compose, so a REST
#     client does store and replay it over http:// and a genuine refresh returns 200.
#
# ─── EXPECTED FAILURES (pre-existing bugs, NOT migration breakage) ───────────
#   • 4.x /users/{id} lets ANY authenticated user read, modify, and delete ANY
#     other user. Section 8 asserts today's (broken) behavior. Fixed in Phase 4.
#   • 5.x /carts/** is fully public with no owner binding. Fixed in Phase 7.
#   • 9.2 the Stripe webhook never updates order status (event-name casing and
#     metadata-key mismatch). Fixed in Phase 8.
#   These are documented so a green run after Phase 4/7/8 — where the assertions
#   flip — is recognized as progress, not regression.
###############################################################################

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

# Fixed credentials so re-runs are predictable.
@userEmail = user@baseline.test
@userPassword = Passw0rd!
@adminEmail = admin@baseline.test
@adminPassword = Adm1nPass!


###############################################################################
# 0. PLATFORM  (actuator + /error dispatch — added in Phase 1)
###############################################################################

### 0.1 Actuator health — expect 200 {"status":"UP"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### 0.2 Actuator liveness group — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health/liveness

### 0.3 Actuator readiness group — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health/readiness

### 0.4 Actuator metrics — expect 401. Only health/info are permitted anonymous;
###     everything else under /actuator stays behind anyRequest().authenticated().
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/metrics


###############################################################################
# 1. REGISTRATION  (public — UserSecurityRules permits POST /users)
###############################################################################

### 1.1 Register the normal user — expect 201 + Location header
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Baseline User",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 1.2 Register the admin user — expect 201
# Still role=USER at this point; seed-baseline.sql promotes it.
# @name registerAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Baseline Admin",
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 1.3 Duplicate email — expect 200 with {"message": "..."} body
# NOTE: DuplicateUserException maps to a plain @ExceptionHandler returning
# ErrorDto with no status override, so this returns 200, not 409. Pre-existing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 1.4 Validation failure — expect 400 with a field->message map
# Blank name, non-lowercase email (custom @Lowercase), 3-char password (min 6).
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "MiXeDCase@baseline.test",
  "password": "abc"
}

### 1.5 Malformed JSON — expect 400 {"message": "Invalid request body"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "name": "broken", }


###############################################################################
# 2. AUTHENTICATION
###############################################################################

### 2.1 Login as the normal user — expect 200 {"token": "..."}
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 2.2 Login as admin — expect 200
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 2.3 Wrong password — expect 401 (empty body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "definitely-wrong"
}

### 2.4 Refresh the access token — expect 200 when the login cookie was stored,
###     400 (MissingRequestCookieException) when it was not. Both fixed in Phase 1:
###     COOKIE_SECURE=false lets the client keep the cookie over http://, and
###     /error is permitted so the 400 is no longer masked as 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh

### 2.5 Current user — expect 200 with the user's UserDto
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@userId = {{me.response.body.$.id}}

### 2.6 Current admin — expect 200, captures the admin's id for section 8
# @name meAdmin
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

@adminId = {{meAdmin.response.body.$.id}}

### 2.7 /auth/me with no token — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 2.8 /auth/me with a garbage token — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.token


###############################################################################
# 3. PRODUCTS  (GET public; POST/PUT/DELETE require ROLE_ADMIN)
###############################################################################

### 3.1 List all products — expect 200, public, no token needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### 3.2 Create a product as ADMIN — expect 201 + Location
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Baseline Widget",
  "price": 19.99,
  "description": "Created by the baseline collection",
  "categoryId": 1
}

@productId = {{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}

### 3.3 Create a second product (needed for multi-item cart tests) — expect 201
# @name createProduct2
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Baseline Gadget",
  "price": 5.50,
  "description": "Second baseline product",
  "categoryId": 2
}

@productId2 = {{createProduct2.response.body.$.id}}

### 3.4 Create as a NORMAL user — expect 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Should Be Rejected",
  "price": 1.00,
  "description": "normal user may not create",
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 3.5 Create with no token — expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Should Be Rejected",
  "price": 1.00,
  "description": "anonymous may not create",
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 3.6 Create with a nonexistent category — expect 400 (empty body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Bad Category",
  "price": 1.00,
  "description": "categoryId 99 is not seeded",
  "categoryId": 99
}

### 3.7 Filter by category — expect 200, only Electronics (categoryId 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?categoryId=1

### 3.8 Update a product as ADMIN — expect 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Baseline Widget (updated)",
  "price": 24.99,
  "description": "Updated by the baseline collection",
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 3.9 Update a nonexistent product — expect 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/999999
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "Ghost",
  "price": 1.00,
  "description": "no such product",
  "categoryId": 1
}


###############################################################################
# 4. USERS  (all authenticated; NO ownership checks today — see section 8)
###############################################################################

### 4.1 List all users — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.2 List sorted by name — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?sortBy=name
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.3 List sorted by email — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?sortBy=email
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.4 Get own user by id — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.5 Get a nonexistent user — expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.6 List users with no token — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### 4.7 Update own profile — expect 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Baseline User Renamed",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}"
}


###############################################################################
# 5. CARTS  (fully public today — CartSecurityRules permits /carts/**)
###############################################################################

### 5.1 Create a cart — expect 201 + Location, no token required
# @name createCart
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts

@cartId = {{createCart.response.body.$.id}}

### 5.2 Add a product to the cart — expect 201 with a CartItemDto
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": {{productId}}
}

### 5.3 Add the same product again — expect 201, quantity increments to 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": {{productId}}
}

### 5.4 Add the second product — expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": {{productId2}}
}

### 5.5 Get the cart — expect 200 with items[] and a computed totalPrice
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}

### 5.6 Update an item's quantity — expect 200
# NOTE: this is POST, not PUT. Unusual, but that is the real route.
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{productId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "quantity": 5
}

### 5.7 Quantity 0 — expect 400 (@Min(1))
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{productId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "quantity": 0
}

### 5.8 Quantity 101 — expect 400 (@Max(100))
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{productId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "quantity": 101
}

### 5.9 Add a nonexistent product — expect 404 "Product not found in the cart"
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": 999999
}

### 5.10 Get a nonexistent cart — expect 404 "Cart not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 5.11 Remove one item — expect 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{productId2}}

### 5.12 Confirm removal — expect 200, that item gone
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}


###############################################################################
# 6. CHECKOUT  (authenticated; needs a non-empty cart + live Stripe test keys)
###############################################################################

### 6.1 Create a fresh cart for checkout — expect 201
# @name checkoutCart
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts

@checkoutCartId = {{checkoutCart.response.body.$.id}}

### 6.2 Put an item in it — expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{checkoutCartId}}/items
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "productId": {{productId}}
}

### 6.3 Checkout — expect 200 {"orderId": N, "checkoutUrl": "https://checkout.stripe.com/..."}
# Requires a valid STRIPE_SECRET_KEY. Without one, expect 500
# {"message": "Error creating a checkout session"} — that is a config problem,
# not a regression. Open checkoutUrl and pay with test card 4242 4242 4242 4242.
# @name checkout
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "cartId": "{{checkoutCartId}}"
}

@orderId = {{checkout.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 6.4 Checkout with no token — expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cartId": "{{checkoutCartId}}"
}

### 6.5 Checkout the now-empty cart again — expect 400 (CartEmptyException)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "cartId": "{{checkoutCartId}}"
}

### 6.6 Checkout a nonexistent cart — expect 400 (CartNotFoundException)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "cartId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### 6.7 Missing cartId — expect 400 (@NotNull)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{}


###############################################################################
# 7. ORDERS  (authenticated; only the caller's own orders)
###############################################################################

### 7.1 List my orders — expect 200 with the order from 6.3
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7.2 Get one order — expect 200, status PENDING (or PAID after a webhook)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7.3 Get someone else's order — expect 403 with an ErrorDto
# The admin did not place this order, so Order.isPlacedBy fails.
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7.4 Get a nonexistent order — expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7.5 List orders with no token — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders


###############################################################################
# 8. ADMIN + AUTHORIZATION MATRIX
###############################################################################

### 8.1 /admin/hello as ADMIN — expect 200 "Hello World"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/hello
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8.2 /admin/hello as normal user — expect 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/hello
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8.3 /admin/hello anonymous — expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/hello

### 8.4 Swagger UI — expect 200 (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui/index.html

### 8.5 OpenAPI spec — expect 200 JSON listing every endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs

### 8.6 Unmapped path — expect 401, not 404
# SecurityConfig ends with anyRequest().authenticated(), so unknown paths are
# rejected before routing. Confirms default-deny is intact.
GET {{baseUrl}}/this/route/does/not/exist

### ⚠️ 8.7 PRIVILEGE ESCALATION — user reads the ADMIN's record
# TODAY: 200 (bug). AFTER PHASE 4: 403. Flipping to 403 is the fix landing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ⚠️ 8.8 PRIVILEGE ESCALATION — user overwrites the ADMIN's profile
# TODAY: 200 (bug). AFTER PHASE 4: 403.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Hijacked By Baseline",
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}"
}

### ⚠️ 8.9 CART HIJACK — anonymous caller reads a cart they do not own
# TODAY: 200 (bug). AFTER PHASE 7: 403 once the cart has an owner.
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}


###############################################################################
# 9. DESTRUCTIVE — run these LAST, they delete the baseline fixtures
###############################################################################

### 9.1 Change password — expect 200
# ⚠️ UserService.changePassword writes the new password WITHOUT bcrypt encoding,
# so 9.2 below currently FAILS with 401. After the Phase 4 fix, 9.2 must pass.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/change-password
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "oldPassword": "{{userPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "NewPassw0rd!"
}

### 9.2 Log in with the NEW password — TODAY 401 (bug), AFTER PHASE 4 expect 200
# This single request proves the plaintext-password bug is fixed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "NewPassw0rd!"
}

### 9.3 Wrong old password — expect 401 (handler catches the wrong exception type)
# UserController imports java.nio.file.AccessDeniedException but the service
# throws org.springframework.security.access.AccessDeniedException, so the
# handler never fires and this surfaces as a 403 from Spring Security instead.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/change-password
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "oldPassword": "wrong-old-password",
  "newPassword": "Whatever1!"
}

### 9.4 Clear the cart — expect 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items

### 9.5 Confirm empty — expect 200, items: [], totalPrice: 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}

### 9.6 Delete a product as ADMIN — expect 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId2}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9.7 Delete a product as normal user — expect 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9.8 Delete a nonexistent product — expect 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9.9 Delete the baseline user — expect 200 (void handler, no explicit status)
# Leaves the DB clean enough to re-run the collection from section 1.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
